From 10d0d89976dc7388fdfa982e6b42fd4fc43e0a29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:11:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Drop agent provenance stamps on Desktop launches

Review of #1776 @447677395a: tool-child stamps (HERMES_AGENT_TOOL_CALL/ORIGIN/HOME)
survived clean_launch_env and the Electron leaked-env scrub, so a Desktop an agent
reopened (update relaunch, desktop command) spawned a HERMES_DESKTOP=1 backend
that the proof-home guard refused on the production home. Drop the stamps in
clean_launch_env, on desktop/gui top-level argv and at Electron startup; serve and
dashboard keep them. Contract test pins the Python and Electron key lists together.
Document that the stamp means "spawned by a Hermes agent process".
